    {
      "id": "sec_s3l7_r1",
      "type": "rule_paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Arabic mein lafz (كُلّ) ka matlab \"har\" (every) hota hai. Lafz (كُلّ) apne baad aane wale Isim se mil kar Murakkab banata hai, jismein baad wala lafz Majroor (kasrah/do zair) hota hai jaise \"كُلُّ كِتَابٍ\" (har kitaab). Quran Kareem ke mandarja zail murakkabat ka tarjuma dekhiye:",
        "content": "Arabic mein lafz (كُلّ) ka matlab \"har\" (every) hota hai. Lafz (كُلّ) apne baad aane wale Isim se mil kar Murakkab banata hai, jismein baad wala lafz Majroor (kasrah/do zair) hota hai jaise \"كُلُّ كِتَابٍ\" (har kitaab). Quran Kareem ke mandarja zail murakkabat ka tarjuma dekhiye:",
